'' '-Os' WITH NO SIZE RUNTIME LINKS THE PLAIN ONE: a library directory without libfb-s.a --
'' the 0.1.7 toolchain's, packaged before the size runtime shipped -- gives its libfb.a, so
'' '-Os' never fails a link '-O2' would make. (Once toolchains/ holds a toolchain that ships
'' libfb-s.a this picks that instead and still passes; it then no longer tests the fallback.)
'' TEST: cli
'' HOSTS: windows
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.osf
'' ARGS: -v -Os --no-module-cache -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/optsize-rt.bas -o build/.osf/a.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64/libfb
'' RUN: build/.osf/a.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: SIZE 42
